comment.narrative:
Based on the findings of the TPM validation report, the achieved target has been revised. Activities conducted include:
• Strengthened the Routine Immunization (RI) system using the zero dose vaccination global and national movement; 
• Deployed various Cold chain equipment to enhance lower-level vaccine cold chain capacity to provide quality immunization services.
• Following stock availability to lower level to avoid stock out; Conducted defaulter tracing in high dropout areas; Conducted EPI program evaluation and woreda prioritization; Conducted integrated demand generation activities which resulted in increased community demand and vaccine uptake;
• The availability of the various policy documents and guidelines pushes the achievement forward. 
• Conducted nationwide health workers capacity building through immunization in practice (IIP) and scaling it up to lower level; Conducted targeted supportive supervision in low performing woredas by national and sub national TAs

