Implementation has been delayed for activities under IPF sub-component I of the Program due to Ministry of Finance counter-funding delays, despite a later waiver by the Bank. However, the activities that have been undertaken include:
Training provided for lower-level health workers;  
Malnutrition Screening conducted; 
Rapid Nutrition Assessments: Conducted in 69 kebeles (26 woredas) in Amhara and 36 kebeles (12 woredas) in Oromia.
• A refresher training on MHPSS was provided to mental health professionals to enhance their skills 
• A comprehensive workshop on Stakeholder and Community Figure Mapping, Advocacy with Stakeholders, and Individual and Group Counselling for MHPSS provision was conducted to support the delivery and integration of mental health services.

