Based on the findings of the TPM validation report, the achieved target has been revised. 
• Conducted Inter-regional forums to strengthen MPDSR activities and referral linkages; 
• Monitored KPIs and supported maternity waiting home initiatives; 
• Supported cesarean section expansion and maternal health service training; Implemented policy orientation, blood bank monitoring, and guideline updates; 
• Conducted mentorship programs; 
• Finalized counseling guides, integrated oxytocin into supply systems, and revised postnatal guidelines; 
• Reviewed maternal health KPIs performances on a quarterly basis and identified Skilled Birth Attendants in low performing regions and provided feedback; 
• Implemented integrated catchment based clinical mentorship program in 8 hospitals; 
• Procured and distributed ultrasound machine to Health centers and provided training to mid-level healthcare providers; 
• Developed postpartum hemorrhage training manual which includes EMOTIVE;

